      "<p>Nimbus Bike Limited (NBL) is a manufacturer of bikes in India. Demand for bikes is high on account of a growing population primarily comprising of youth in the age group of 18-30 years. NBL is the second largest bike manufacturer in India. Competition is stiff in a market where the customers are highly price sensitive.</p> <p>Until now the company has been following a standard costing methodology to understand and manage costs. The management determines cost standards that need to be met and reviews them annually. However, despite the MIS reports indicating that the cost variances are under control and are not unfavorable to the company, NBL&rsquo;s bikes are not cost competitive in the market. Therefore, Tarun Kumar the current CEO of the company wants to explore the concept of using Kaizen costing understand and manage costs. Currently the cost of manufacturing is RS 60,000 per bike. On adopting the Kaizen costing methodology, the management has set of goal of achieving a 1% cost reduction in the next month that is July 2026.</p> <p>While discussing on the ways to achieve the 1% cost reduction target, following are the suggestions received from different employees:</p> <ul> <li>Raj an engineer in the design department suggests that if a particular part of the bike&rsquo;s engine can be redesigned, the time required to assemble the bike can reduce by 0.1% of the current time taken.</li> <li>Stanley the procurement manager suggests switching to another supplier, which will enable NBL procure the component at the same quality but at lower price.</li> <li>Chatur the production manager suggests revamping the entire production and assembly line that can increase the scale of production.</li> <li>Ankur in the paint shop suggests improvements to the bike painting process that will reduce set up time while paining bikes of different colors i.e. SMED (Single-Minute Exchange of Die).</li> </ul> <p>In order to make the Kaizen method more effective, NBL is going to adopt the 5S methodology of improving its operations. Following are some of the measures that are suggested:</p> <p>Measure 1. Remove unnecessary items from the assembly line in order to reduce the risk of installing the wrong component.</p> <p>Measure 2. Arrange tools in &ldquo;shadow boards&rdquo; so that workers easily access the tools and instantly know where they belong while replacing them.</p> <p>Measure 3. Clean the workstation daily to remove any clutter, improve workplace safety, inspect machines and tools to ensure that they function properly.</p> <p>Measure 4. Standardize processes to streamline workflow and enhance efficiency.</p> <p>Measure 5. Periodic staff training, daily monitoring and fixing accountability for allocated areas in the workspace.</p> <p>After implementation of the Kaizen costing methodology, the actual cost reduction was `500 per bike for the month of July 2026.</p> <p><strong>Match the following</strong></p> <table> <tr> <th>S NO</th> <th>Measure</th> <th>S NO</th> <th>5S </th> </tr> <tr> <td>i</td> <td>Remove unnecessary items from the assembly line in order to reduce the risk of installing the wrong component.</td> <td>a</td> <td>Seiketsu</td> </tr> <tr> <td>ii</td> <td>Arrange tools in “shadow boards” so that workers easily access the tools and instantly know where they belong while replacing them. </td> <td>b</td> <td>Seiri</td> </tr> <tr> <td>iii</td> <td>Clean the workstation daily to remove any clutter, improve workplace safety, inspect machines and tools to ensure that they function properly. </td> <td>c</td> <td>Shitsuke </td> </tr> <tr> <td>iv</td> <td>Standardize processes to streamline workflow and enhance efficiency.</td> <td>d</td> <td>Seiton </td> </tr> <tr> <td>v</td> <td>Periodic staff training, daily monitoring and fixing accountability for allocated areas in the workspace. </td> <td>e</td> <td>Seiso</td> </tr> </table>",
